            <ArticleTitle>The reversal of epidural morphine induced somnolence with physostigmine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>678-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two case reports are presented of patients with post-thoracotomy pain treated with epidural morphine who developed somnolence several hours after the procedure. Physostigmine, 1 mg IV successfully reversed the somnolence without any effect on analgesia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
